<title>MEXICO: Mexico's Vector gains permission to trade futures.</title>
<headline>Mexico's Vector gains permission to trade futures.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-01-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's Vector brokerage said in a statement on Monday it had been granted provisional permission to trade futures in the local financial markets on nominal interest rates and the consumer price index.</p>
<p>Futures trading in Mexico was authorized in October 1994 and began in April 1995.</p>
<p>Officials from the Mexican Stock Exchange told Reuters that Vector could begin to trade futures during the second quarter of 1997.</p>
<p>((--Mexico City newsroom +525 728-9554))</p>
</text>
